abstract: >-
  EvalMORAAL is a moral-alignment evaluation framework for large language
  models that combines chain-of-thought (CoT) elicitation with LLM-as-
  judge peer review. Evaluating 20 models against the World Values Survey
  (64 countries) and PEW Global Attitudes Survey (27 topics, 5 repetitions
  per cell), we find that explicit CoT reasoning consistently improves
  alignment over implicit log-probability scoring, while peer-review
  judging by GPT-4o reproduces human preferences more reliably than naive
  aggregation. A persistent Western / non-Western gap remains across model
  families and scales.
